    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23YPHZgtrQdmM3x3d757z7z)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Problem (after #487):** the author works report takes about 10 s before its tables show.\n- **Cause:** not Org tables. Building the report text is fast; the slow part is `org-table-widget-mode`, which `sp-textui` turns on for every Org buffer (`org-mode-hook`). It lays out each table as its own widget (overlays, pixel measuring), about 10 to 20 ms per table, and the report has one table per author.\n- **Fix:** batch reports keep plain Org tables. `sp-batch-report--quiet-table-widget` on `sp-batch-report-mode-hook` turns the widget off; it runs while the buffer is still empty, so it costs nothing. The tables are already padded in Lisp (#487), so they look aligned without it.\n- **Opt back in:** `sp-batch-report-table-widgets` non-nil (slow for many tables).\n- Docs are bullet lists (`sp-batch-report.org`); `.el` matches. `when-let*` only; no CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Timings (Emacs 29.3 batch, synthetic data, widget forced in a terminal window; the GUI measures pixels too, so it is slower there)\n\n| Tables x rows | Before (widget on) | After (widget off) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 20 x 10 | 0.45 s | 0.01 s |\n| 120 x 10 | 1.80 s | 0.06 s |\n| 300 x 20 (6000 rows) | 9.95 s, 6600 overlays | 0.37 s, 0 overlays |\n\n- Text build alone for 6000 rows: 0.4 s; `font-lock-ensure` 0.07 s; one `org-table-align` 0.01 s.\n- **Not measured:** the GUI and your real BibTeX data (no access to your machine from this session). The 300-table case matching your 10 s is the evidence, not a profile of your Emacs.\n- **Tests:** `sp-batch-report-test` 23 pass (1 new: the widget is off in a report, on with the option); `sp-author-notes-bibtex-test` 16 pass.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 492-batch-report-no-table-widget; git checkout 492-batch-report-no-table-widget`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex`: the tables show within a second or two after the reading is done (time it; it was about 10 s)\n- [ ] The tables are plain aligned `|` text (no widget borders), headings fold with `TAB`\n- [ ] `RET`, `o`, `c`, `C`, `d`, `u`, `g` still work on rows\n- [ ] `d` / `u` / `g` redraw quickly too\n- [ ] `M-x customize-variable sp-batch-report-table-widgets` to `t`, run the report again: widgets are back (and slow); set it to nil again\n- [ ] Other Org buffers (a normal note with a table) still show table widgets\n- [ ] Optional: `M-x profiler-start` before the command and `M-x profiler-report` after, to see if anything else is slow\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`\n- Optionally `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 492-batch-report-no-table-widget`\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAF6gJZsaMTJLEA9cM)_",
